35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The data is stark. Eighteen members never show up, yet a quarter of us do two-thirds of the work. This imbalance is unsustainable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Six hours a month chasing individual payments. That is not a job, it is a punishment. We need a structure that respects the next person’s time.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The sign-in sheets confirm my fear. A quarter of us do two-thirds of the work, while eighteen never appear. The rota shows the same nine doing everything.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, the data confirms it. A door charge killed our weekday turnout. People stopped feeling those evenings were theirs. We need to restore that sense of belonging.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, your six hours are a disaster. But the ledger is worse. Seventy percent of costs are fixed, billed whether we show up or not. We can’t just guess.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the winter social feedback is worrying. Three quiet members feel uneasy about the cost per visit. We must protect that low-pressure entry point.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, the fixed costs are the real trap. If seventy percent is unavoidable, we cannot afford the administrative chaos of chasing individual payments.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the administrative chaos is real, but so is the resentment. The same nine carry the physical load. We need a structure that acknowledges that burden, not just the paperwork.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, the taster forms are damning. Nine of fourteen refused a whole-year commitment. We are scaring people off before they even start.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, nine out of fourteen? That’s a massive leak. If we scare them off, we lose the income we need to cover those fixed costs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, the imbalance is undeniable. But if we punish the quiet ones, we lose the newcomers who might become regulars. We need a structure that protects both.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, resentment is valid, but I cannot hire a full-time accountant. We need a system that minimizes the chasing, not just the guilt.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But a system that ignores the physical labor will just burn out the same nine. We need to value their time, not just the paperwork.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the physical labor is real, but the hesitation is killing us. If we make people feel like guests, they won’t come. We need to fix the vibe, not just the books.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, you’re right. Chasing payments is a nightmare. But we can’t ignore the fixed costs. We need a fee that covers the hall and insurance without the headache.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, I agree. We need a system that is simple to administer but fair to those who barely attend. Let’s see the options.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, simplicity is the only way to keep the books sane. I am ready to see which option actually respects the next treasurer’s time.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, simplicity helps the books, but it ignores the people doing the heavy lifting. I need a structure that acknowledges the physical burden, not just the paperwork.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the physical burden is real, but the hesitation is killing us. If we make people feel like guests, they won’t come. We need to fix the vibe, not just the books.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, agreed. Simplicity is key. But we must ensure the fee covers those fixed costs without bankrupting the quiet members. Let’s see the options.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
