60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, Option A is the only one that protects the quiet members and keeps administration simple. I am voting for the flat annual fee.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Six hours a month chasing payments is unacceptable. Option C is administrative suicide. I am voting for the flat annual fee.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I hear the administrative pain, but a flat fee ignores the nine carrying the physical load. I am voting for Tiered Membership.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, tiers create the exact friction that killed our weekday turnout. We need to remove the hesitation, not add labels. I am voting for the flat annual fee.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, you’re right. Chasing payments is a nightmare. Option A is the only way to cover those fixed costs without the headache. I’m voting for the flat annual fee.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, tiers create the very labels that make newcomers feel like outsiders. We need to protect that low-pressure entry point. I stand by my vote for the flat fee.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, I respect the concern, but tiers invite the friction we just saw in the minute books. Simplicity is the only way to keep the books sane. I stand by my vote for the flat fee.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the minute books show friction, but the rota shows burnout. A flat fee ignores the physical labor. I stand by my vote for Tiered Membership.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the hesitation is the real killer. Tiers just add more labels to a system people already dread. I stand by my vote for the flat fee.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
